WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.200
2022's "Scream" pays tribute to "Scream" by&nbsp;
bringing back characters from "Scream" to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.840
face the killer from "Scream" all over again.&nbsp;
Screaming yet? This is the ending of the fifth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.600
"Scream" movie, "Scream," explained.
 
"I've seen this movie before."&nbsp;

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.676
"Not this movie, Sydney."

00:00:15.676 --> 00:00:19.840
The film kicks off with a very typical set-up:&nbsp;
Tara Carpenter is home alone when a stranger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:24.400
starts calling her landline phone. Shocker --&nbsp;
the new Ghostface has found his first victim.&nbsp;

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.400
When Tara's estranged sister Sam gets a call&nbsp;
from Wes Hicks about the attack on Tara,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.760
she hotfoots it to her hometown with&nbsp;
her helpful boyfriend Richie in tow.&nbsp;

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.320
When she's arrived, she's quickly interrogated&nbsp;
by Tara's fiercely protective best friend Amber.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:41.360
To be fair, Amber's suspicions make sense; Sam&nbsp;
conveniently comes home the day after Tara is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.760
attacked? It seems too good to be true.
Resident film nerds Chad and Mindy are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.600
quick to point out Ghostface is involved,&nbsp;
and anyone could be behind the mask -- even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.120
the main character.
"We're all suspects."&nbsp;

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:57.600
We find out that Sam left Woodsboro because&nbsp;
she uncovered a dark family secret: She's the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:02.400
secret daughter of Billy Loomis, and suffers&nbsp;
from hallucinatory visions of Billy himself.&nbsp;

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.800
"What's the matter, Sydney? You&nbsp;
look like you've seen a ghost."&nbsp;

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:08.960
What do you do when a new Ghostface&nbsp;
starts hunting your family and friends?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:14.000
Well, you get help from someone with expertise, of&nbsp;
course. Enter, Dewey Riley. The washed up former&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.400
sheriff lives alone in his trailer, separated&nbsp;
from Gale Weathers. He helps the new class of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:22.880
victims establish that the killer is trying to&nbsp;
make his own 'requel' -- a reboot-slash-sequel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.200
which is why the new killer is going after&nbsp;
anyone connected to the previous killing sprees.&nbsp;

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:31.920
Ghostface even slaughters "Scream 4" alum Judy&nbsp;
Hicks and her son Wes in a stunningly tense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.880
sequence set inside the Hicks' house.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:38.640
Look, it just wouldn't be a legacy sequel&nbsp;
if one of the original characters didn't die&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:42.720
in a sacrificial blaze of glory. The&nbsp;
film is all about passing the torch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:46.160
so obviously a fan-favorite character&nbsp;
has to meet their end at some point.&nbsp;

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:50.160
Gale Weathers is the second legacy character&nbsp;
to show up in the film, arriving in Woodsboro&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:54.320
to cover the news for her successful morning&nbsp;
show. Although she divorced Dewey after "Scream&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:58.240
4," they reunite at the Hicks house, which&nbsp;
gives them the opportunity to resolve the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:03.440
issues that drove them apart. Oh, no. Character&nbsp;
development? You can see where this is going.&nbsp;

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:07.520
Ghostface obviously doesn't stop with the Hicks'&nbsp;
family, making their way to the hospital where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:11.440
Tara is recovering so they can finish the job&nbsp;
they started in the film's opening. Thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:16.080
Dewey shows up, shooting Ghostface in the chest&nbsp;
several times so Sam can get Tara to safety.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:20.320
But as soon as he steps into the hallway, he's&nbsp;
practically signed his own death sentence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:25.120
The killer butchers Dewey with two knives, ripping&nbsp;
his abdomen and back to shreds until he bleeds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.840
out on the floor. Rest in peace, Dewey.
Thankfully, Gale has Sidney to lean on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:34.720
for support -- which is surprising, since they've&nbsp;
always had an uneasy relationship over the years.&nbsp;

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:38.320
While all this is happening, the teenagers&nbsp;
are holding a remembrance party for Wes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:42.000
in Stu Macher's old house -- the place&nbsp;
where the original finale happened.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.560
It wouldn't be "Scream" without a party now,&nbsp;
would it? But then most of the partygoers leave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:50.800
after realizing that just by the act of being&nbsp;
there, they're practically begging to be killed.&nbsp;

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:52.720
"Sounds about right."

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:56.080
Chad is attacked by Ghostface, while&nbsp;
various members of the group like Liv,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.840
Tara, and Richie go missing. But this is&nbsp;
"Scream" we're talking about, so there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:04.000
are always going to be plenty of red herrings&nbsp;
for the audience to over-analyze. Thankfully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:08.320
fans don't have to wait long for resolution,&nbsp;
because in a moment of extreme paranoia in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:14.160
group Amber whips out a gun and executes Liv at&nbsp;
point blank range. "Welcome to Act 3," indeed.&nbsp;

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:18.640
But who's her accomplice? Well, the writers&nbsp;
cleverly subvert a typical trope in the franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:23.680
because surely it can't be the main character's&nbsp;
boyfriend again, can it? Actually yes it can,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:28.800
as Richie outs himself to Sam, Sidney, and Gale as&nbsp;
Amber's accomplice. In typical "Scream" fashion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:33.680
the two killers wax lyrical about their motives,&nbsp;
and it's just about as meta as you'd expect.&nbsp;

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:37.840
Turns out, Amber and Richie are both disgruntled&nbsp;
fans of the "Stab" franchise -- you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:41.360
the movie-series-within-a-movie that's&nbsp;
based on the events of the original movie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:45.200
They bonded online over their shared hate&nbsp;
for the most recent film, "Stab 8," before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:49.040
coming up with the idea for their own movie.
Amber and Richie go on their killing spree so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:52.800
the "Stab" franchise has fresh source&nbsp;
material to work with going forward.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:57.280
By creating their own Ghostface, the duo hopes to&nbsp;
essentially shape the narrative of the next film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:00.000
believing that their ideas for a&nbsp;
sequel are better than anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.880
the studio will come up with. In Richie's own&nbsp;
words, "Someone has to save the franchise."&nbsp;

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:09.520
"That was so f—ing stupid. Pure horsesh-t. The&nbsp;
death of horror, right here in front of us."&nbsp;

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:12.880
It's a clever maneuver from the writers,&nbsp;
who are clearly taking pot-shots at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:17.360
specific fandoms in the real world who go on&nbsp;
mass-hate campaigns when specific movies and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.760
sequels aren't to their liking.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:23.200
Although Amber and Richie feel like they've&nbsp;
created a victim-proof plan to frame&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:27.040
Sam as the new killer in their "Stab" 'requel',&nbsp;
they don't account for the fact that she has an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:31.360
inner darkness that is personified by the&nbsp;
Billy Loomis hallucinations. It's a clever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:35.440
way of turning the deadly Loomis legacy into&nbsp;
something positive, as Sam tells Richie he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:39.120
shouldn't "[mess] with the daughter of a serial&nbsp;
killer," before stabbing him over, and over.&nbsp;

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:44.080
"I'll be right b-ahaha."
"Hahaha. He's dead."&nbsp;

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:48.880
Amber doesn't get away either, as Sidney and&nbsp;
Gale tag team the teenage killer in the kitchen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:52.800
knocking her back so she face-plants on&nbsp;
the lit stovetop, setting her on fire.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:57.600
It's a horrifying fate for the disillusioned&nbsp;
student, but it's also some sweet revenge for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:02.320
Gale. Since this is "Scream," we're all expecting&nbsp;
the killers to get back up for one final scare,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:05.760
but we get yet another subversion&nbsp;
here, as Sam unloads several shots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:10.320
into Richie's bloody body before that happens.
Out of the new cast, there's a healthy batch of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:14.000
survivors -- with Tara, Sam, Chad,&nbsp;
and Mindy all making it out alive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.200
After everything Sidney and Gale have been&nbsp;
through over the years, they both deserve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:21.680
a happy ending -- although Gale makes a point of&nbsp;
saying she's not going to write about the killers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:25.520
No, this time she's going to write about Dewey.&nbsp;
She's arrived at a point where she doesn't need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:30.480
to memorialize the evil in the world; Gale's&nbsp;
ready to honor those who always try to do good.&nbsp;

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:33.534
Now that's what we call character development.

